  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A plan with «ir a»",
     "texto": [
      "To talk about a plan, use **ir a + infinitive**:\n\n- **Voy a** viajar.\n- **Vas a** estudiar.\n- **Vamos a** comer.\n\nOnly the verb **ir** changes: **voy, vas, va, vamos, vais, van**. The second verb **never changes**: it always stays in the infinitive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Ir in the present + a + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **ir** is irregular:\n\n- yo **voy**\n- tú **vas**\n- he, she, usted **va**\n- we **vamos**\n- you plural (vosotros) **vais**\n- they, ustedes **van**\n\nAfter it always comes **a** and an **infinitive**: **voy a comer**, **van a viajar**. With **llover** and other weather verbs there is no subject: **va a llover**."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
